ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
  Alternate vertices considered: packet fibers, sidecar bundles, quotient maps,
  denominator transports, endpoint events, Haar rectangles, charge reservoirs,
  deletion decks, and theorem exits.
  Preserved predicate: whether a primitive packet exits by q-witness, AP/GW
  boundary, petal/K33 named debt, positive-open covering mass, or a new
  zero-open kernel.
  Destroyed if naively quotiented: height/flex, endpoint owner, exact period,
  off-grid floor, and the transverse Qsqrt(-7) sidecar.

BOTTOM LINE
  The strongest new route is not another scalar.  It is a first-failure
  theorem: enlarge the actual-packet sheaf until residue-word exactness fails;
  prove no such failure, or show the first failure is exactly height/flex,
  owner-current, tropical off-grid floor, exact-period, or named K33/H7
  debt.  HYP-3402 and HYP-3403 make owner-current/tropical-wall plus
  shadow-charge packet gluing the first handoffs before harder Hessian
  or curvature routes.  This would convert
  the current creative stack into a rigorous labelled-packet theorem target.
